  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 紙\ntitle: paper\njlpt: 4\ntags: [jlpt-n4, grade-2, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 10\nradical: 糸\nradicalNumber: 120\nonyomi: [シ]\nkunyomi: [かみ]\ndistractors: [終, 私, 後]\n---\n\n# 紙 — paper\n\n**Strokes:** 10 · **Key (radical):** 糸 (no. 120) · **JLPT:** N4 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n紙 means paper, both as the word [紙](../words/紙.md) (かみ) and in words for paper products and written materials.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic, not verified etymology:** picture the thread-shaped 糸 at the left tying up sheets\nof paper marked with the angular 氏 shape on the right. No historical role for either component is asserted here.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| シ | on | 用紙 ようし — paper; blank form |\n| かみ | kun | [紙](../words/紙.md) かみ — paper |\n| がみ | kun, voiced in compounds | 手紙 てがみ — letter; 折り紙 おりがみ — origami |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [紙](../words/紙.md) かみ — paper\n- 手紙 てがみ — letter\n- 用紙 ようし — paper for a use; blank form\n- 折り紙 おりがみ — origami; paper folding\n\n## Notes\n\nThe がみ in 手紙 is a voiced form of かみ, not a separate on reading.\n髪 (かみ, hair) and 神 (かみ, god or deity) have the same kana spelling but different meanings and kanji.\n\n[終](終.md) shares the 糸 left side. [私](私.md) also has an on reading シ, but means \"I\" or \"private,\" not paper.\n\nDictionary data: [KANJIDIC2 and JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/) (J. W. Breen / EDRDG; [CC BY-SA 4.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)).\n",
